10643	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T16:23:47.727Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers s2's ac4–ac6 and the mandatory ER definition.","evidence":"The stored DEF assigns s2 the common read shape, empty lifecycle parts, references and parent-derived children. These map to readWithHistory, decoder defaults and childrenOf. The stored LLD contains an erDefinition with Artifact, the lifecycle family, Actor, Reference, history, feedback, TaskSet, Task and RepoSchema, including ownership relationships. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"Retain this coverage while resolving the contract gaps below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"writeArtifact currently preserves revisions for identical writes and meta-only writes, carries tracker metadata on content writes, and atomically replaces the head.","evidence":"The complete writer calls sameApartFromRevision, carries meta.tracker through carryTracker, copies the prior revision for meta-only writes, and writes JSON through writeAtomic. The existing tests explicitly cover these behaviors. Identical comparison currently excludes only top-level meta.revision. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-writer.test.ts]","action":"Preserve these exact semantics in the extraction; distinguish them from the new store's content classification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The four gates readers are synchronous JSON readers with ArtifactMissingError for absent files.","evidence":"Each complete reader uses existsSync, readFileSync and JSON.parse without promises. requireApprovedEpic, requireApprovedHld, requireApprovedLld and requireApprovedPlan consume their results synchronously and inspect the existing metadata. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"Keep the synchronous wrappers and return the original parsed head to existing callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The s1 identity API exists with strict parsing and a parent-key function suitable for reuse.","evidence":"ArtifactIds.parse validates by round-tripping through make and rejects uppercase story ids. parentOf returns an ArtifactKey: TASK/TASKS/DIAG map to STORY, STORY maps to EPIC, and other kinds return undefined. [files: src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts]","action":"Compare parent.entityId with ArtifactIds.make(parentKey), and explicitly handle undefined parents.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed common store and decoder are new capabilities rather than existing implementations being duplicated.","evidence":"Source searches found no ArtifactStore, decodeArtifactHead, RepoSchemaGate or WriteJournal implementation. Reading storage.ts, gates.ts and provenance/writer.ts confirmed separate head writing, per-type JSON readers and body.feedback mutation, rather than the proposed common envelope/history API. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/provenance/writer.ts]","action":"Reuse the existing primitives through the proposed adapters.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The creation contract supplies enough context for codecs to construct metadata required by existing readers and renderers.","evidence":"ArtifactMetaBase requires workflow, runId, repoPath, createdAt, elapsedMs, repoIndexedAt and schemaVersion. The design names encode(payload, ctx), but does not define ctx or how write(a, by) obtains these fields when no prior head exists. The anchor helpers do not supply workflow-run provenance. Insrc analysis discovery was unavailable; direct reads established the requirements but found no proposed context-provider contract. [files: src/workflow/types.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/define.ts, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2.json]","action":"Specify the codec context type, its constructor/provider, and how each kind obtains required creation metadata. Include a create-without-prior-head test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Renaming the provenance ChangeLogEntry and ChangeLog types can preserve the BUILD record's stored shape.","evidence":"collectBuildChangeLog emits target, author and timestamp; StandaloneBuildRecord stores the resulting array in body.changeLog; changeLogBodyLines reads target, author, timestamp and optional summary. None serializes the TypeScript type name. Searches also identified type imports in three test files. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/provenance/types.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/format/bindings.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/provenance-build.test.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/provenance/__tests__/types.test.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/format/__tests__/bindings.test.ts]","action":"Rename the production and test imports together without altering serialized fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Flat amendments can remain untouched until s9 while existing amendment commands continue using them.","evidence":"proposeAmendment writes the record directly with JSON.stringify(record); readAmendment and transition validate the flat AmendmentRecord. The actual AMD-7 file has top-level id, amendment and status, with no meta/body envelope. [files: src/workflow/amendments/store.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-7.json]","action":"Keep the existing amendment path independent until the coordinated conversion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Declaring the lifecycle and tracker shapes unchanged, while deferring their behavior, respects the approved ownership boundaries.","evidence":"HLD sc4 assigns lifecycle transitions, hashing and roll-up to s3; sc6 assigns tracker binding behavior to s6. The LLD's listed fields match those sketches and explicitly defer those behaviors. The prefix/suffix extension is explicitly required by binding requirement 5. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"Preserve the exact HLD field types when implementing the abbreviated sketches.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The readWithHistory contract addition is approved for downstream consumption.","evidence":"AMD-7 contains the stated sc2 methodAdd, so the claim that it was filed is correct. Its status is 'pending'. approvedInApplyOrder explicitly filters for status === 'approved', so it is not part of the effective approved contract yet. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-7.json, src/workflow/amendments/store.ts]","action":"Resolve AMD-7 before treating the extended sc2 interface as approved.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified journal record is sufficient to recover the original logged operation after an append failure or restart.","evidence":"The LLD persists only '{ operationId, priorRevision, bytes }'. HLD sc3 requires each ChangeLogEntry to contain 'actor' and 'timestamp'. For a metadata-only write, the actor passed as by need not appear in the staged head because lifecycle is persisted as supplied. After a crash before append, recovery cannot reconstruct the original actor or timestamp. Further, an identical-head write whose append fails meets the recovery condition 'head already equals the staged bytes', causing clear-only recovery despite the missing log entry. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2.json, .insrc/artifacts/HLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Stage the complete immutable ChangeLogEntry with the prepared head. On recovery, ensure that entry is appended idempotently even when head bytes already match, then replace the head if needed and clear the journal. Test restart before append, a different retry actor, and an identical-head append failure.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion assigned to s2 has a named proving test in the design.","evidence":"The actual DEF assigns ac4, ac5 and ac6 to s2. The LLD maps them respectively to combined history/envelope reads and round trips, empty lifecycle reads, and reference/parent/children tests. Existing artifact-writer and inventory tests provide relevant regression controls; the proposed tests are plans, not executed evidence. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s2.json, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-writer.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-write-inventory.test.ts]","action":"Retain the acceptance mapping and add the recovery tests identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-20T16:23:47.727Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
